{"id": "SmoothNonconvexNonEuclidean", "contribution": null, "title": "SmoothNonconvexNonEuclidean.lean", "filename": "SmoothNonconvexNonEuclidean.lean", "modifiedAt": "2026-10-14T11:59:40+00:00", "stale": true, "catalog": {"problem_class": [{"label": "nonconvex", "details": "Unconstrained optimization of an everywhere Fréchet differentiable function f:E→ℝ; convexity is not required. The derivative satisfies ‖Df(x)−Df(y)‖≤L‖x−y‖. There exists a global lower bound lower with f(x0)−lower≤Δ. All parameters, including E, L>0, Δ≥0, ε>0, and x0, are public; f is the instance.", "evidence": "LongTails/Setups/SmoothNonconvexNonEuclidean.lean: Params; spec.Public, publicInput, Instance, valid, admissible."}], "oracle": [{"label": "exact_gradient", "details": "Each query x returns the exact Fréchet derivative Df(x), a continuous linear functional E→ℝ. Exactness holds for every call index and seed by uniqueness of the derivative. No function values or oracle errors are supplied.", "evidence": "LongTails/Setups/SmoothNonconvexNonEuclidean.lean: spec.Query, Reply, and first two conjuncts of admissible."}], "distinctive_assumptions": [{"label": "non_euclidean_geometry", "details": "E is an arbitrary complete real normed space with a measurable-space structure, potentially infinite dimensional. No inner product or additional geometric assumption is imposed. Smoothness and stationarity use the operator norm on the dual space E*.", "evidence": "LongTails/Setups/SmoothNonconvexNonEuclidean.lean: Params.normedE, linearE, completeE, measurableE; spec.Reply, admissible, successful."}], "accuracy": [{"label": "gradient_norm_squared", "details": "The output X takes values in E and must satisfy E[‖Df(X)‖²]≤ε², using the continuous-linear-functional operator norm. X must be measurable and its squared derivative norm integrable.", "evidence": "LongTails/Setups/SmoothNonconvexNonEuclidean.lean: spec.Output and successful."}, {"label": "expected", "details": "The guarantee is an expectation under the supplied probability measure P. In Convergence, P is the product of the algorithm and oracle seed laws; no deterministic or almost-sure accuracy guarantee is required.", "evidence": "LongTails/Setups/SmoothNonconvexNonEuclidean.lean: spec.successful; LongTails/Template.lean: Convergence."}], "setup_category": {"label": "non_standard", "reason": "The formulation requires smooth nonconvex stationarity over arbitrary real Banach spaces, with dual-valued derivative access and no additional geometry. This generality extends beyond the usual Euclidean or Hilbert-space benchmark."}, "schema_version": 2, "proof_status": {"status": "missing_theorem", "theorems": [], "verification": "not_checked_by_catalog"}, "literature_status": {"status": "not_assessed", "results": []}}, "descriptionHtml": "<h2 class=\"unnumbered\" id=\"smooth-nonconvex-banach-space-optimization\">Smooth Nonconvex\nBanach-Space Optimization</h2>\n<p>We consider minimizing a possibly nonconvex function <span class=\"math inline\" data-tex=\"\\(f:E\\to\\mathbb{R}\\)\"><mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"CHTML\" style=\"font-size: 113.1%; position: relative;\"><mjx-math class=\" MJX-TEX\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D453 TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\" space=\"4\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c3A\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\" space=\"4\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D438 TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\" space=\"4\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c2192\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo><mjx-TeXAtom space=\"4\" texclass=\"ORD\"><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-ds mjx-b\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c211D TEX-A\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi></mjx-TeXAtom></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable=\"on\" display=\"inline\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mo>:</mo><mi>E</mi><mo accent=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">→</mo><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mi mathvariant=\"double-struck\">R</mi></mrow></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container></span> on a real Banach space\